\f0\fs69\fsmilli34667 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Physical Humans-Robot Interaction Accessibility Guidelines (PHRIAG)
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs53\fsmilli26667 \cf0 Purpose\'a0
\f2\b\fs48 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 These guidelines are to ensure accessible interactions in mixed human-robot environments. This includes service and industrial robots that operate in public and private settings. We combine ideas from automation, engineering, and robotics \'96 e.g. International Organization for Standardization (ISO) \'96 and accessibility, primarily web/digital accessibility.
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs53\fsmilli26667 \cf0 Defining Accessibility
\f2\b\fs48 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 We operationalize \'93accessibility\'94 by drawing from the principles outlined by Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.w3.org/WAI/fundamentals/accessibility-principles/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 W3C}}). The first 4 principles of HRIAG align with web accessibility defined by WCAG (Perceivable, Operable, Understandable, and Robust). We define these principles in the context of human-robot interactions. Additional principles of pHRIAG are not covered by digital definitions of accessibility but align with robots as physically embodied.
\f1\fs24 \
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\b\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Perceivable:
\f0\b0  Communication from the robot and any user interface components must be presentable to users in ways they can perceive (e.g. communication signals must be perceiveable by users with different dis/abilities.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f3\b\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Operable:
\f0\b0  User interface components must be operable such that a human can safely use & interact with the robot (e.g. people with mobility or physical disabilities must be able to open the delivery robot compartment.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f3\b\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Understandable:
\f0\b0  Communication from robots and the operation of any user interface must be understandable to the user (e.g. legible robot motion.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f3\b\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Robust:
\f0\b0  Robots must be algorithmically and physically robust (i.e. adaptive) to operate in a 
\f3\b range of environments
\f0\b0  AND i
\f3\b nteract with diverse human populations
\f0\b0 . Furthermore, they must be robust enough to be interpreted reliably by a wide variety of users with different dis/abilities.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Compatible\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\pardeftab720\li2160\fi-2160\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl2\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 With people\'92s current accessibility tools.\
