\fs53\fsmilli26667 \cf0 Defining Disability
\f2\b\fs48 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 We also operationalize disability in the context of accessibility. Disability can be long-term/permanent or short-term/temporary. A 
\f3\b long-term disability 
\f0\b0 can be one a person is born with or acquired during the duration of their lives (ie, ). For example, people who have a visual, mobility, or hearing disability in everyday life. A 
\f3\b short-term disability 
\f0\b0 is one a person may have temporarily for a few weeks or months. This can be due to an illness or injury. A 
\f3\b \'93situational\'94 impairment 
\f0\b0 arises from the specific context a person is in; for example, momentarily having your vision occluded during driving, or being in a loud environment in which they cannot hear quiet sounds.
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 Scholars note that disability is not simply defined by one\'92s medical diagnosis but \'93the social norms that define particular attributes as impairments, as well as the social conditions that concentrate stigmatized attributes in particular populations.\'94 ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jstor.org/stable/48671434?seq=3"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Minich, 2016}}). Here, these models are broadly divided into a 
\f3\b medical model of disability
\f0\b0 , which focuses on disability as an \'93impairment\'94 needing to be cured ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/1878803.1878807"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Mankoff, 2010}}); and a 
\f3\b social model of disability
\f0\b0 , which views disability as an identity on top of a person\'92s \'93impairment\'94, which society uses to socially exclude people with disabilities ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://d1wqtxts1xzle7.cloudfront.net/32344952/Davis_Reader_social_model-libre.pdf?1391626454=&response-content-disposition=inline%3B+filename%3DThe_social_model_of_disability.pdf&Expires=1756751278&Signature=aqI4XmCQQl44Kj9NMl32W7eiWRUHnsaUz7a4GFgkeWoxDN4tlp5cbyo9pFK~kBvXfNHQlqrIKOKB6kN3-uKL2Ztrm3CagunvJhW5N7wEbKLfkM6otjy0Hazsv9-zkfLMywL1EUVKZk8e0gH8XI7bQ11aXC9kZiqUggzYzG-S4KDgokxkmLg60GnkTbQagyBfRC1JOwYtK7nGVs21CwaLgrfvIlOZrGbgpGXYqBfLKXdJMz8lZAJ0TBDOHT5BVDirm87UO1GKIL-Fj2Zs6~f68YAYLu-J9tg8TQ4M6zEvrbfHjGrniUA3diB6AZJG21duPOZQqy5UlaM-cWGgY4zuLg__&Key-Pair-Id=APKAJLOHF5GGSLRBV4ZA"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Shakespeare, 2006}}).
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

