\f0\fs42\fsmilli21333 \cf0 Service Robots
\f2\b\fs36 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li480\fi-480\sa106\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf0 Definition
\f2\b\fs28 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 A service robot (SR) is one that is for \'93personal use or professional use that 
\f3\b performs useful tasks
\f0\b0  for humans or equipment" ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:std:iso:8373:ed-3:v1:en"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 ISO 8373:2021}}). 
\f3\b Personal use
\f0\b0  tasks include \'93handling or serving of items, transportation, physical support, providing guidance or information, grooming, cooking and food handling, and cleaning.\'94
\f3\b  Professional use tasks
\f0\b0  include \'93inspection, surveillance, handling of items, person transportation, providing guidance or information, cooking and food handling, and cleaning.\'94
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 Some examples include autonomous delivery robots used for e-commerce last-mile delivery; or social robots used for personal wellbeing tasks. Other examples include \'93Agriculture Robots,\'a0 Construction Robots, Customer Service Robots,\'a0 Defense Robots Demolition, Robots Exoskeleton, Robots Field Robots, Humanoid Robots, Industrial Cleaning Robots, Inspection Robots, Logistics Robots, Medical Robots\'94({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.automate.org/robotics/service-robots/what-are-professional-service-robots"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Association for Advancing Automation Robotics}}).\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\
\
